                    \\array{
                    p(y) &amp; \stackrel{1}{\to} &amp; p(y) \\
                    \\mathllap{p(h)} \downarrow &amp;  &amp; \downarrow \mathrlap{p(h)} \\
                    \\mathllap{p(r(k))} &amp; \stackrel{1}{\to} &amp; \mathrlap{p(r(k))}\\
                    \\mathllap{\theta_k} \downarrow &amp; &amp; \downarrow \mathrlap{p(\epsilon_k)} \\
                    x &amp; \underset{k}{\to} &amp; p(e).
                    }
            %p
              In other words, the universal property provides a unique
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mi k
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi h
                    %mo =
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon_k \circ h = g
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi θ
                        %mi k
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi h
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta_k \circ p(h) = f
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon_k
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+arrow"} cartesian arrow
            %p
              Thus, the existence of a right adjoint to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              means precisely that for each morphism
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi x
                      %mo →
                      %mi p
